<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Block Diffusion NELBO</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we provide the Negative ELBO (NELBO) for the block diffusion parameterization. Recall that the sequence <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}=\left[{\mathbf{x}}^{1},\dots,{\mathbf{x}}^{L}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}=\left[{\mathbf{x}}^{1},\dots,{\mathbf{x}}^{L}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is factorized over <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> blocks, which we refer to as <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity, drawn from the data distribution <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we will factorize the likelihood over <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> blocks of length <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then perform diffusion in each block over <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> discretization steps. Let <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the Kullback-Leibler divergence, <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,s</annotation></semantics></math> be shorthand for <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)=i/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)=i/T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(i)=(i-1)/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(i)=(i-1)/T</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i\in[1,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i\in[1,T]</annotation></semantics></math>. We derive the NELBO as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\prod_{i=1}^{T}{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s(i)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(i)},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{\prod_{i=1}^{T}q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(i)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s(i)})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\prod_{i=1}^{T}{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s(i)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(i)},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{\prod_{i=1}^{T}q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t(i)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s(i)})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{b=1}^{B}\bigg[\underbrace{-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>recons</mtext></msub></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{b=1}^{B}\bigg[\underbrace{-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{2}{T},\dots,\frac{T-1}{T},1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>D</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{2}{T},\dots,\frac{T-1}{T},1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>D</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub></munder><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Masked BD3-LMs</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We explore a specific class of block diffusion models that builds upon the masked diffusion language modeling framework. In particular, we focus on masking diffusion processes introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. (2021)</a></cite> and derive a simplified NELBO under this framework as proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we define the diffusion matrix <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for states <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,V\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,V\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the noise schedule function <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a strictly decreasing function in <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the mask index as <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=V</annotation></semantics></math>. The diffusion matrix is defined by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al. (2021)</a></cite> as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[Q_{t}]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }i=j=m\\
\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }i=j\neq m\\
1-\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }j=m,i\neq m\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[Q_{t}]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }i=j=m\\
\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }i=j\neq m\\
1-\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }j=m,i\neq m\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The diffusion matrix for the forward marginal <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[Q_{t|s}]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }i=j=m\\
\alpha_{t|s}&amp;\text{if }i=j\neq m\\
1-\alpha_{t|s}&amp;\text{if }j=m,i\neq m\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[Q_{t|s}]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }i=j=m\\
\alpha_{t|s}&amp;\text{if }i=j\neq m\\
1-\alpha_{t|s}&amp;\text{if }j=m,i\neq m\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t|s}=\alpha_{t}/\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t|s}=\alpha_{t}/\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Forward Process</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the D3PM framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, the forward noise process applied independently for each token <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,\dots L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,\dots L\}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined using diffusion matrices <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t};\overline{Q}_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}\right),\quad\text{with}\quad\overline{Q}_{t(i)}=Q_{t(1)}Q_{t(2)}\dots Q_{t(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t};\overline{Q}_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}\right),\quad\text{with}\quad\overline{Q}_{t(i)}=Q_{t(1)}Q_{t(2)}\dots Q_{t(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Reverse Process</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the diffusion matrix for the forward marginal. We obtain the reverse posterior <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}\mid{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}\mid{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> using the diffusion matrices:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\frac{q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}{q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}{{({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t})}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\frac{q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}{q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}{{({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t})}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Hadmard product between two vectors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Simplified NELBO for Masked Diffusion Processes</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we simplify the NELBO in the case of masked diffusion processes. Below, we provide the outline of the NELBO derivation; see the full derivation in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will first focus on simplifying the diffusion loss term <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#A1.Ex1" title="In Appendix A Block Diffusion NELBO ‣ Block Diffusion: Interpolating Between Autoregressive and Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. We employ the SUBS-parameterization proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024b)</a></cite> which simplifies the denoising model <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> for masked diffusion. In particular, we enforce the following constraints on the design of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> by leveraging the fact that there only exists two possible states in the diffusion process <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\in\{{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell},{\mathbf{m}}\}\;\forall\ell\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\in\{{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell},{\mathbf{m}}\}\;\forall\ell\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Zero Masking Probabilities</span>. We set <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math> (as the clean sequence <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> doesn’t contain masks).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Carry-Over Unmasking</span>. The true posterior for the case where <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1</annotation></semantics></math> (if a token is unmasked in the reverse process, it is never remasked). Thus, we simplify the denoising model by setting <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">As a result, we will only approximate the posterior <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a token in the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th position in block <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\{1,\dots,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\{1,\dots,B\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The diffusion loss term becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{D}_{\text{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{D}_{\text{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply the discrete-time diffusion loss for the block <math id="A2.Ex8.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>; hence, from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a></cite> (Suppl. B.1), we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, we obtain a tighter approximation of the likelihood by taking the diffusion steps <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>, for which <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})=\alpha_{t}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})=\alpha_{t}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For the continuous time case, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a></cite> (Suppl. A.2.4) show the reconstruction loss reduces to 0 as <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t(1)}^{b}\sim\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\text{Cat}\left(.;{\mathbf{x}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b}\right)=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{x}}^{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t(1)}^{b}\sim\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\text{Cat}\left(.;{\mathbf{x}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b}\right)=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{x}}^{b})</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>recons</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t(1)}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t(1)}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t(1)}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t(1)}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The prior loss <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}=\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}=\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> also reduces to 0 because <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t=1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t=1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> which ensures <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\mathbf{x}}_{t=1}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{x}}_{t=1}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t=1}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t=1}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a></cite> (Suppl. A.2.4).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we obtain a simple objective that is a weighted average of cross-entropy terms:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{BD}}({\mathbf{x}};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{BD}}({\mathbf{x}};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The above NELBO is invariant to the choice of noise schedule <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024a)</a></cite> (Suppl. E.1.1).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Recovering the NLL from the NELBO for Single Token Generation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the block diffuson NELBO for a block size of 1 where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}=1,B=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}=1,B=L</annotation></semantics></math>. The block diffusion NELBO is equivalent to the AR NLL when modeling a single token:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log p({\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log p({\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex13.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because\alpha_{t}^{\prime}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∵</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because\alpha_{t}^{\prime}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Ex13.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=1-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=1-t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{1}{t}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{1}{t}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\frac{1}{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\frac{1}{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex16.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Expanding <math id="A2.Ex16.m1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}[.]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}[.]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\frac{1}{t}\bigg[q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\frac{1}{t}\bigg[q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 80.00012pt+q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 80.00012pt+q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that our denoising model employs the SUBS-parameterization proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024b)</a></cite>. The “carry-over unmasking” property ensures that <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, as an unmasked token is simply copied over from from the input of the denoising model to the output. Hence, (<a href="#A2.Ex12" title="In B.4 Recovering the NLL from the NELBO for Single Token Generation ‣ Appendix B Masked BD3-LMs ‣ Block Diffusion: Interpolating Between Autoregressive and Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) reduces to following:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\frac{1}{t}q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\frac{1}{t}q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex19.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\because q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∵</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\because q({\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t}={\mathbf{m}}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})=t</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}={\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For single-token generation (<math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) we recover the autoregressive NLL.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Tightness of the NELBO</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For block sizes <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq K\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq K\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that -<math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p({\mathbf{x}})\leq\mathcal{L}_{K}\leq\mathcal{L}_{K+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p({\mathbf{x}})\leq\mathcal{L}_{K}\leq\mathcal{L}_{K+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, where we recover the autoregressive NLL (see Suppl <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Recovering the NLL from the NELBO for Single Token Generation ‣ Appendix B Masked BD3-LMs ‣ Block Diffusion: Interpolating Between Autoregressive and Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consider the ELBO for block size <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{2}=\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{2}=\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We show that <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{1}\leq\mathcal{L}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{1}\leq\mathcal{L}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and this holds for all <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq K\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq K\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> by induction. Let <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to the token in position <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[1,L^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[1,L^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math> of block <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. We derive the below inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{b=1}^{L}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{m}},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\prod_{i=1}^{2}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\prod_{i=1}^{2}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\prod_{i=1}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\log\prod_{i=1}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{b=1}^{L/2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{1}{1-\alpha_{t}}p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Specialized Attention Masks</h3>

<div id="A2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to model conditional probabilities <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{x}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math> for all blocks <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in[1,B]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in[1,B]</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously by designing an efficient training algorithm with our transformer backbone. However, modeling all <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> conditonal terms requires processing both the noised sequence <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math> and the conditional context <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rather than calling the denoising network <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> times, we process both sequences simultaneously by concatenating them <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{full}}\leftarrow{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\oplus{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{full}}\leftarrow{\mathbf{x}}_{t}\oplus{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> as input to a transformer. We update this sequence <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{full}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{full}}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens using a custom attention mask <math id="A2.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{full}}\in\{0,1\}^{2L\times 2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{full}}\in\{0,1\}^{2L\times 2L}</annotation></semantics></math> for efficient training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The full attention mask is comprised of four <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\times L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\times L</annotation></semantics></math> smaller attention masks:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{full}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathcal{M}_{BD}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{OBC}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{BC}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{full}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathcal{M}_{BD}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{OBC}\\
\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{BC}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{BD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{BD}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{OBC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{OBC}</annotation></semantics></math> are used to update the representation of <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{BC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{BC}</annotation></semantics></math> is used to update the representation of <math id="A2.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define these masks as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{BD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{BD}</annotation></semantics></math> (Block-diagonal mask): Self-attention mask within noised blocks <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{M}_{BD}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $i,j$ are in the same block}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext> are in the same block</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{M}_{BD}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $i,j$ are in the same block}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{OBC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{OBC}</annotation></semantics></math> (Offset block-causal mask): Cross-attention to conditional context <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{M}_{OBC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mtext> belongs in a block before </mtext><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{M}_{OBC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{BC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{BC}</annotation></semantics></math> (Block-causal mask): Attention mask for updating <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{M}_{BC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in the same block as $i$, or a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mtext> belongs in the same block as </mtext><mi>i</mi><mtext>, or a block before </mtext><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{M}_{BC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in the same block as $i$, or a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We visualize an example attention mask for <math id="A2.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=6</annotation></semantics></math> and block size <math id="A2.SS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}=2</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ B.6 Specialized Attention Masks ‣ Appendix B Masked BD3-LMs ‣ Block Diffusion: Interpolating Between Autoregressive and Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="261.17" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 486.34 261.17" width="486.34"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,261.17) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(26.08,0) translate(0,24.81)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFE6CC;--ltx-fill-color:#FFE6CC;--ltx-fg-color:#FFE6CC;" color="#FFE6CC" fill="#FFE6CC" fill-opacity="0.7" stroke="#FFE6CC" stroke-opacity="0.7"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 236.22 M 0 236.22 L 0 118.11 L 118.11 118.11 L 118.11 236.22 Z M 118.11 118.11"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF8000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF8000;--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" color="#FF8000" fill="#FF8000" stroke="#FF8000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 236.22 M 0 236.22 L 0 196.85 L 39.37 196.85 L 39.37 236.22 Z M 39.37 196.85"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF8000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF8000;--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" color="#FF8000" fill="#FF8000" stroke="#FF8000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 39.37 196.85 M 39.37 196.85 L 39.37 157.48 L 78.74 157.48 L 78.74 196.85 Z M 78.74 157.48"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF8000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF8000;--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" color="#FF8000" fill="#FF8000" stroke="#FF8000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 78.74 157.48 M 78.74 157.48 L 78.74 118.11 L 118.11 118.11 L 118.11 157.48 Z M 118.11 118.11"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFFF;" color="#CCFFFF" fill="#CCFFFF" fill-opacity="0.7" stroke="#CCFFFF" stroke-opacity="0.7"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 118.11 236.22 M 118.11 236.22 L 118.11 118.11 L 236.22 118.11 L 236.22 236.22 Z M 236.22 118.11"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#00FFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#00FFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#00FFFF;" color="#00FFFF" fill="#00FFFF" stroke="#00FFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 118.11 196.85 M 118.11 196.85 L 118.11 118.11 L 157.48 118.11 L 157.48 196.85 Z M 157.48 118.11"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#00FFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#00FFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#00FFFF;" color="#00FFFF" fill="#00FFFF" stroke="#00FFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 157.48 157.48 M 157.48 157.48 L 157.48 118.11 L 196.85 118.11 L 196.85 157.48 Z M 196.85 118.11"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFCC;" color="#FFFFCC" fill="#FFFFCC" fill-opacity="0.7" stroke="#FFFFCC" stroke-opacity="0.7"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 118.11 118.11 M 118.11 118.11 L 118.11 0 L 236.22 0 L 236.22 118.11 Z M 236.22 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFF00;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFF00;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFF00;" color="#FFFF00" fill="#FFFF00" stroke="#FFFF00"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 118.11 118.11 M 118.11 118.11 L 118.11 0 L 157.48 0 L 157.48 118.11 Z M 157.48 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFF00;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFF00;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFF00;" color="#FFFF00" fill="#FFFF00" stroke="#FFFF00"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 157.48 78.74 M 157.48 78.74 L 157.48 0 L 196.85 0 L 196.85 78.74 Z M 196.85 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFF00;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFF00;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFF00;" color="#FFFF00" fill="#FFFF00" stroke="#FFFF00"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 196.85 39.37 M 196.85 39.37 L 196.85 0 L 236.22 0 L 236.22 39.37 Z M 236.22 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 236.22 0 M 0 19.69 L 236.22 19.69 M 0 39.37 L 236.22 39.37 M 0 59.06 L 236.22 59.06 M 0 78.74 L 236.22 78.74 M 0 98.43 L 236.22 98.43 M 0 118.11 L 236.22 118.11 M 0 137.8 L 236.22 137.8 M 0 157.48 L 236.22 157.48 M 0 177.17 L 236.22 177.17 M 0 196.85 L 236.22 196.85 M 0 216.54 L 236.22 216.54 M 0 236.21 L 236.22 236.21 M 0 0 L 0 236.22 M 19.69 0 L 19.69 236.22 M 39.37 0 L 39.37 236.22 M 59.06 0 L 59.06 236.22 M 78.74 0 L 78.74 236.22 M 98.43 0 L 98.43 236.22 M 118.11 0 L 118.11 236.22 M 137.8 0 L 137.8 236.22 M 157.48 0 L 157.48 236.22 M 177.17 0 L 177.17 236.22 M 196.85 0 L 196.85 236.22 M 216.54 0 L 216.54 236.22 M 236.21 0 L 236.21 236.22 M 236.22 236.22"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.38 -18.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="14.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 51.75 -18.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="14.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 91.12 -18.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="14.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 130.49 -18.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="14.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 169.86 -18.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="14.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F3.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 209.23 -18.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.26" ov